# Routes AI-bundle changes to the skill that knows all four gate seams.
#
# CLAUDE.md states the failure directly: "The AI-bundle gate has four seams — change
# all or none. buildMcpConfig, installAiDefaultsMcpTools, componentInstallationOrchestrator
# and handleRegenerateAiFiles each apply the same predicate. Miss one and creation and
# regenerate silently produce different bundles."
#
# Silent, and split across a creation path and a regeneration path that are separate
# call chains — only one of which the flow you are testing exercises.
rule_id=ai-bundle
rule_once=1

rule_match() {
    case "$1" in
        Edit|Write) ;;
        *) return 1 ;;
    esac
    [ -n "$3" ] || return 1
    case "$3" in
        */services/aiBundle/*) return 0 ;;
        */handlers/*RegenerateAiFiles*) return 0 ;;
    esac
    return 1
}

rule_message() {
    cat <<'MSG'
You are changing what Demo Builder writes into a project's AI bundle. Invoke the
`ai-context-authoring` skill (Skill tool, skill: "ai-context-authoring") first.

The gate has FOUR seams and they must change together — `buildMcpConfig`,
`installAiDefaultsMcpTools`, `componentInstallationOrchestrator` and
`handleRegenerateAiFiles` each apply the same predicate. Miss one and project
CREATION and "Regenerate AI Files" produce different bundles, silently, because
they are separate call chains and your test almost certainly drives only one.

Existing projects are the other half: a bundle change that only works for NEW
projects is half a change. That is what AI_CONTEXT_VERSION and the activation
sweep are for, and the skill carries the bump discipline.

This hook fires only once per session.
MSG
}
